   "kind": "document",
   "title": "Statistics Exercise Guide",
   "text": "Problem 2: Conditional Probability with Cards\nQuestion. Two cards are drawn without replacement from a standard 52-card deck. What is the probability that both are aces?\nSolution. The first card is an ace with probability 4 / 52. Given that, three aces remain among 51 cards, so P(second is ace | first is ace) = 3 / 51. Multiply: (4 / 52) * (3 / 51) = 12 / 2652, about 0.0045. Because the draws are without replacement the events are not independent, so we must use the conditional probability.",
